  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recent hires. And nearly 4 in 10 employers \nsaid they now actively prefer older workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over recent grads even after accounting for \nthe expectation of higher salaries. Now again,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568320,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every generation of managers in history has \ncomplained that their new hires are soft,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the specific nature of the complaint this \ntime is different. These workers have spent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their entire lives being coddled in the role of \nstudent and consumer, which meant every awkward  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decision was handled for them long before they \never had a first day on the job. Both of those  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roles have been aggressively re-engineered over \nthe last two decades to remove every possible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moment of ambiguity. Teachers grade on rubrics \nthat are published in advance. Learning apps  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596320,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tell people exactly which button to press next. \nDating apps remove the awkward human element of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600800,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "approaching someone in person. Food delivery apps \nremember your order. And investment apps round up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your spare change and invested on your behalf. \nUnironically, many consumers report feeling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overwhelmed by the choice of what piece of content \nto watch on their preferred streaming service. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they just give up and go back to scrolling through \ncontent that is picked for them. And I mean,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619680,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I personally want to sound superior to this \npoint, but I have absolutely done this myself.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every single one of these improvements has \nquietly removed a moment where a person used to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have to stop, figure something out, and decide for \nthemselves. Then on day one of their actual job,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635760,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somebody hands them a task with no rubric, no \ntutorial, no autoplay, and no obvious right  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640960,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "answer, and asks them to go and figure it out, \nwhich feels like a character flaw right up until  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you realize it's the exact behavior their entire \nupbringing rewarded. And the really awkward bit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for employers is that being genuinely good \nat just figuring things out is genuinely one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the most valuable skills anybody can bring \nto any career. It is the exact thing managers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have usually trusted humans over software to do. \nBecause software by its nature still struggles  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a problem it hasn't seen before. Although \nunfortunately if the studies are to be believed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672640,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are simultaneously getting worse at this \nwhile the clankers are getting better. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677280,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more on that later, which brings us to the second \nproblem, and it starts much earlier than anybody's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683200,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first job. The iPad Kid meme has started being a \nmeasurable phenomenon. Across the developed world,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689200,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a clear trend of declining, but more \nimportantly, diverging test scores. The OECD's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "latest piece of results showed that math scores \nacross its member countries fell by roughly 15  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700160,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "points between 2018 and 2022. That was the single \nlargest consecutive drop since the test was first  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "administered. Now, even though this did fit into \na longerterm trend, the larger than average drop  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could have been written off as one-time effects \nof COVID teaching from home. But the concerning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715600,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "detail was that these test scores didn't fall \nevenly. The NAP found that the top performing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722080,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "students largely held their ground while the \nbottom performing students fell off a cliff,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suggesting that the convenience economy isn't \ndragging everybody down equally. It is dragging  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down the kids with the least ability to push back \nagainst it. The remote learning shakeup didn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "affect all students equally either. For advanced \nand already disciplined students, it was largely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741520,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fine. A quiet room and a laptop let them learn \nat their own pace without classroom distractions.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For underperforming students, well, it gave \nthem much easier access to Fortnite instead.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "User-friendly and highly engaging technology is \ngenerally hard to snap yourself out of, even for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757840,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fully grown adults who should in theory have \nbetter self-control than a teenager. Actually,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "removing these distractions takes either serious \nself-discipline or serious parental discipline.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for a lot of households, that second one is a \nluxury they simply cannot afford. A single parent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "working two jobs is not going to police screen \ntime the same way a wealthier household can when  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778080,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can afford a stay-at-home parent, private \ntuition, or a school that has banned phones  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entirely. So, the class gap compounds. Wealthier \nkids are more likely to end up in environments  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that still make them figure things out. Everybody \nelse is more likely to end up in environments  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791680,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explicitly designed to never ask them to. And \nthen on top of all of this, we have AI, which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the third and probably the biggest of these \ncompounding problems. In theory, large language  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "models are a genuinely powerful learning tool for \na disciplined student or professional. They can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explain a concept a dozen different ways, simulate \ntutoring, and take a lot of the drudgery out of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812480,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real knowledge work. Sure, they like to make a lot \nof [ __ ] up on the fly, but so do regular human  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818240,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "educators, and some models can be asked to provide \nsources and citations along the way. In practice,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824080,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, that's not really how most people have been \nusing them. The Digital Education Council's 2024  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829920,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "survey found that 86% of university students now \nuse generative AI in their studies and separate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "research from best colleges found that more than \nhalf of them used it specifically to cheat an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assignment or an exam. Teachers trying to catch \nthis are fighting an arms race they are quietly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losing because the detection tools are themselves \nwrong enough to be effectively useless in a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "disciplinary setting, which has led to an entire \ncohort of students passing through school without  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854400,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever doing the exact activity that used to build \nthe figuring things out muscle in the first place.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the job market has gone through a mirror image \nof the same thing. Applicants use AI to fire off  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundreds of customized résumés and cover letters \na week. Employers respond by running their own AI  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "filters over the resulting flood of applications, \nrejecting most of them before a human ever sees  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875120,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them. The end result is a hiring process \nwhere a machine is writing the application,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another machine is reading it, and a real human \nis just getting a polite email saying, \"We have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decided to go in another direction.\" And while all \nof this is happening, AI is being sold to schools  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a cost-effective way to replace teachers and to \ncompanies as a cheap way to replace their junior  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workers who would on a normal career path have \nbeen the ones actually doing the work that teaches  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people how to figure things out. Every layer of \nthe system that used to teach people how to think  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through an unfamiliar problem is being quietly \nremoved and sold back to us as progress. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910480,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is an obvious fix to almost all of this. You \ncould put friction back in harder curricula with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no open book policies. Phones out of school, \nreal consequences for AI cheating, hiring  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921840,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "processes that involve an actual human reading \nan actual piece of work from an actual candidate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "financial products that actually make you look \nat what you are spending before you spend it, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "programs that prioritize functionality over ease \nof use. Almost none of this is going to happen,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the reasons why are not mysterious. The market \nrewards the frictionless product and any single  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "business that tries to add friction back in loses \ninstantly to a competitor that doesn't. Parents  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannot win a technology war against companies \nwith literal billions of dollars and teams of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "behavioral scientists engineered specifically to \nkeep their kids engaged. Regulators who, to put  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it generously, are at least a generation older \nthan the technology they are meant to regulate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have no real framework for any of this. but that \nthere is a school system that's going to start  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966720,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "um making sure that first graders or even preks \nhave A1 teaching, you know, every year starting,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, that far down in the grades. And that's \njust a that's a wonderful thing. And budget cuts  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979360,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to public schools mean that every education system \nis leaning harder into AI, not less, because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a chatbot that costs nothing will always win the \nline item fight against a human teacher that costs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990160,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a salary. From the market's point of view, things \nare already working exactly as intended. And if  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want further proof of that, go and watch \nthis video next to find out how we are slowly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "becoming unemployable. And don't forget to like \nand subscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
